LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Beyond the Name Tag: Making Every Conversation Count at America's
  Role in the World Conference
DESCRIPTION:What Is This Workshop?  Taking place exactly one week before 
 the America's Role in the World (ARW) conference\, this session is an int
 eractive "insider playbook" designed to build your physical muscle memory
  for high-stakes professional networking.  Instead of sitting through a s
 tandard presentation\, you will spend two hours in a hands-on workshop en
 vironment learning how to talk about your background naturally\, receivin
 g real-time coaching\, and gaining the confidence to navigate any room or
  reception with senior leaders\, diplomats\, and industry executives.  Wh
 at You'll Get Out of ItIcebreaking Mechanics &amp\; Follow-Up: Master sim
 ple\, proven frameworks for starting a high-impact conversation\, asking 
 smart questions\, making a memorable impression\, and executing post-conf
 erence follow-ups.    Talk About Your Work Like a Professional: Stop desc
 ribing your classes like homework. Learn how to take standard papers\, re
 search\, or group projects and translate them into 30-second conversation
 al insights that prove you understand real-world policy and global issues
 .    Live Reception Simulation: Participate in a simulated high-stakes ne
 tworking reception. Practice entering active conversation circles with vi
 siting executives\, holding your ground\, and making clean\, professional
  exits.    Real-Time Coaching &amp\; Feedback: Receive immediate\, low-st
 akes feedback on your delivery and conversation flow in small-group lab r
 otations.    Bounce-Back Strategies: Gain actionable tradecraft tactics f
 or handling awkward interactions\, recovering from "networking fails\," a
 nd turning brief encounters into long-term professional connections.     
      Open to all undergraduate and graduate students (Freshmen through Ph
 D candidates) across international affairs\, public policy\, cybersecurit
 y\, data science\, and related disciplines.    Preparation: No prior netw
 orking experience required—just bring an idea of one paper\, class proj
 ect\, or campus activity you've worked on recently!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4 data-path-to-node="11">  What Is This Wo
 rkshop?</h4><p data-path-to-node="12">  Taking place exactly one week bef
 ore the <strong data-path-to-node="12" data-index-in-node="41">America's 
 Role in the World (ARW)</strong> conference\, this session is an interact
 ive "insider playbook" designed to build your physical muscle memory for 
 high-stakes professional networking.</p><p data-path-to-node="13">  Inste
 ad of sitting through a standard presentation\, you will spend two hours 
 in a hands-on workshop environment learning how to talk about your backgr
 ound naturally\, receiving real-time coaching\, and gaining the confidenc
 e to navigate any room or reception with senior leaders\, diplomats\, and
  industry executives.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="15">  What You'll Get Out
  of It</h4><ul data-path-to-node="16"><li><p data-path-to-node="16\,0\,0"
 ><strong data-path-to-node="16\,0\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Icebreaking 
 Mechanics &amp\; Follow-Up:</strong> Master simple\, proven frameworks fo
 r starting a high-impact conversation\, asking smart questions\, making a
  memorable impression\, and executing post-conference follow-ups.    </p>
 </li><li><p data-path-to-node="16\,1\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="16\,1
 \,0" data-index-in-node="0">Talk About Your Work Like a Professional:</st
 rong> Stop describing your classes like homework. Learn how to take stand
 ard papers\, research\, or group projects and translate them into 30-seco
 nd conversational insights that prove you understand real-world policy an
 d global issues.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="16\,2\,0"><strong 
 data-path-to-node="16\,2\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Live Reception Simula
 tion:</strong> Participate in a simulated high-stakes networking receptio
 n. Practice entering active conversation circles with visiting executives
 \, holding your ground\, and making clean\, professional exits.    </p></
 li><li><p data-path-to-node="16\,3\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="16\,3\,
 0" data-index-in-node="0">Real-Time Coaching &amp\; Feedback:</strong> Re
 ceive immediate\, low-stakes feedback on your delivery and conversation f
 low in small-group lab rotations.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="1
 6\,4\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="16\,4\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Boun
 ce-Back Strategies:</strong> Gain actionable tradecraft tactics for handl
 ing awkward interactions\, recovering from "networking fails\," and turni
 ng brief encounters into long-term professional connections.    </p></li>
 </ul><ul><li><p data-path-to-node="22\,0\,0">      Open to all undergradu
 ate and graduate students (Freshmen through PhD candidates) across intern
 ational affairs\, public policy\, cybersecurity\, data science\, and rela
 ted disciplines.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="22\,1\,0"><strong 
 data-path-to-node="22\,1\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Preparation:</strong>
  No prior networking experience required—just bring an idea of one pape
 r\, class project\, or campus activity you've worked on recently!    </p>
 </li></ul>
